Therefore, the main ingredients which need to be established beyond reasonable doubt are:
a) Firstly, that the accused was driving the vehicle on a public road;
b) Secondly, that the accused was driving the vehicle in a rash or negligent manner as to endanger human life;
c) Thirdly, that grievous hurt has been caused due to the rash or negligent driving of the accused.
